# .dockerignore — exclude dev/test/scratch files from the production image.
#
# Why this matters: the previous Dockerfile did `COPY . .` which shipped
# the entire backend tree — including server.py (a no-auth open proxy),
# stress_*.py (auth-bypass load testers), refresh_*.py (dev-only token
# refreshers), and the entire scratch/ directory — into the production
# image. Anyone with RCE on the running container (or with shell access
# via `docker exec`) could run them. This file ensures the image only
# contains the application code, the entrypoint, and its runtime
# dependencies.

# --- Dev-only / load-test / open-proxy scripts ---------------------------
# server.py was an unauthenticated OpenAI-compatible proxy on port 8888.
# It is deleted from the repo in PR 16. The pattern below catches it in
# case it's ever reintroduced by a copy-paste.
server.py
*_proxy.py
nous_proxy.py
nous_openai_proxy.py
token_proxy.py

# Stress / load / bypass scripts. These are intentionally meant to bypass
# auth and rate limits for load testing; they must never reach prod.
stress_*.py
stress_*.sh
limits_bypass.py

# Dev token-refresh scripts. The backend uses the live OAuth flow in
# production; these scripts are for local Hermes auth.
refresh_*.py
refresh_*.sh
generate_device_code.py
current_token.sh
watchdog.sh

# --- Scratch / one-shot DB scripts ---------------------------------------
# These are committed for reference but should never run inside the
# production container. They typically assume a developer's local Supabase
# project and would either fail noisily or, worse, succeed silently and
# mutate production data in unexpected ways.
scratch/

# --- Tests ---------------------------------------------------------------
# Pytest tests must not be in the prod image — they pull in pytest,
# response-mock libs, etc. as transitive deps and double the image size.
tests/
.pytest_cache/
.ruff_cache/
htmlcov/
.coverage

# --- Python build / cache artifacts --------------------------------------
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
*$py.class
*.so
.Python
.venv/
venv/
env/
*.egg-info/
build/
dist/

# --- Git / IDE / OS noise -----------------------------------------------
.git/
.gitignore
.gitattributes
.github/
.editorconfig
.vscode/
.idea/
*.swp
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db

# --- Docs and changelogs (no runtime value) ------------------------------
*.md
docs/
CHANGELOG.md

# --- Local env / secrets ------------------------------------------------
# .env* files are NEVER copied into images. Production secrets come from
# Railway runtime env injection only.
.env
.env.*
!.env.example

# --- Generated / runtime artifacts --------------------------------------
*.log
*.pid
*.sock
.cache/
.tmp/
tmp/

# --- Type stubs / mypy cache --------------------------------------------
.mypy_cache/
.pyright_cache/
*.pyi
